Sonata: Mission Control (scale) tells sonata2 what is done to a window,
through ipc-rules' custom events: a right click asks for its app menu
(sonata-scale-menu#, the Dock's menu), a drag starts and drops
(sonata-scale-drag#: dropped on a desktop of the desktops bar, or on +,
the window goes there), the window under the pointer and where it's
drawn (sonata-scale-hover#: its close button). A click where no window
is closes it; a window comes off its place after DRAG_OFF_PX, not 200 px.
sonata2/shell/spaces.py, mission.py, dock_menu.py

